{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\nThe user said: \"Read the CAMPAIGN.md file in your agent folder and start your research campaign.\" CAMPAIGN.md (campaign-6, opus-5-5) sets the task:\n- Build a price-simulation model for Synth SN50 with the lowest CRPS across three configurations: CRYPTO_24H (BTC, ETH, SOL, XRP, HYPE; 24h horizon, 5-min steps, 289 points), COM_EQU_24H (XAU, NVDAX, GOOGLX, TSLAX, AAPLX, WTIOIL, SPCX, SP500; SPYX is dead, ignore it), and CRYPTO_1H (the crypto assets; 1h horizon, 1-min steps, 61 points).\n- The model is measured over the 10 days after the 2026-10-11 data cutoff. Judge every experiment on CRPS, never on field position.\n- Budget: $100 and 18 hours. Read agent/BUDGET.md at every iteration; a LANDING ORDER in it is non-negotiable. Hardware: 14 CPU, 48 GB RAM, one T4 GPU (one GPU job at a time).\n\nHard constraints, kept verbatim in substance:\n- No lookahead. Treat everything after 2026-10-11 as nonexistent. Querying any API (scores, rewards, dashboard) for times after 2026-10-11 is forbidden.\n- Prices come only from the snapshot (market_data/, read-only). Never fetch market data online; the web is for knowledge only. Event dates come only from the calendar at $SYNTH_BENCHMARK_CALENDAR, read inside simulate() through the env var. Tolerate a missing file, type or date.\n- Scoring goes through synth_lib.backtester (via agent/predict.py). Never reimplement the metric.\n- Never falsify the journal or results. Never copy another miner's served paths.\n- Keep binary and encoded data out of the terminal: never cat parquet, npy, bundles or weights; never pipe base64.\n- Use public sources only. If any operator miner models turn up, leave them unread and note them in suggestions.md.\n- simulate(asset, start_time, time_increment, time_length, num_simulations, context_prices) returns (start_timestamp, time_increment, *paths). Each path has time_length//time_increment+1 floats and starts at the last context price. context_prices is a minute DataFrame (open, high, low, close, volume, trade_count) that may contain NaN: drop NaN, never interpolate. Honour num_simulations (1000 in serving). Must run offline.\n- If the model uses randomness, seed every generator from SYNTH_BENCHMARK_SEED, with a fallback seed when the variable is absent.\n- Run everything with `uv run` from the workspace root.\n- Do not backtest across the structural breaks (2026-06-23, 2026-03-11, 2026-09-22 for 1h — use --latest-formula, ~07-17 SPYX/SP500).\n\nDeliverables in agent/:\n- journal.md: one entry per iteration (Hypothesis / Change / Result / Verdict / Lesson).\n- report.md: explainer for Synth miners covering context, approach, experiments including failures, results, limitations, and what I would do with more budget.\n- suggestions.md.\n- CHAMPION: YAML with sha (an existing commit), agent_dir: agent, profiles [low, high], and notes giving backtested CRPS per configuration at 1000 paths plus the starter's CRPS.\n- Commit everything to git before the deadline.\n- A champion is mandatory. Nominating is final: stopping while CHAMPION exists ends the campaign. Keep iterating until there is evidence that further work won't help, or a landing order arrives.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n- **Validator CRPS (synth.validator.crps_calculation).** Each interval's returns are scored in bps.\n  - 24h: 288 5-min returns, 48 30-min, 8 3-hour, and one absolute 24h price normalised by the last price ×1e4. Rough weight: 5-min ~61%, 30-min ~25%, 3h ~10%, 24h ~4%.\n  - 1h: 1-min (measured 26%), 2-min (18.5%), 5-min (12%), 15-min (7%), 30-min (5%), 60-min abs (3.5%), 12 \"gap\" intervals of cumulative return from 0 to 5k minutes (28%), and a volatility CRPS on block std with λ=5.25 (only ~1% of the score).\n- **Field structure.** ASSET_COEFFICIENTS: SP500 3.44 and AAPLX 2.09 are the highest. The per-prompt \"best\" is a minimum over ~240 miners, so it is biased low. The fair comparison is against the best single miner's mean CRPS.\n- **Offline bundle.** Scored prompts span 2026-09-08 → 2026-10-11. 24h prompts arrive about hourly at odd minutes; 1h prompts about every 10 minutes.\n- **Validation windows.** W_A = 09-12→09-26 and W_B = 09-26→10-11. For 1h runs, B is shortened to 10-01→10-11 for speed. Experimental profiles are fitted on data before 09-08.\n- **Context timing.** The context ends at start − (lead 60s for 1h / 120s for 24h) − 60s (context_end).\n- **Model.**\n  - Variance per minute = weekly profile (New York local time, 15-min bins, 7×96) × deseasonalised level.\n  - The level comes from gap-aware EWMAs of overlapping step-minute returns on the forward-filled last-traded price; ffill is used for estimation only and never served.\n  - The forecast decays from the short EWMA into the long one.\n  - Path increments are Student-t, scaled by a per-path lognormal vol multiplier (ETA), with an atom at zero for unchanged prices, and a martingale correction.\n- **Profile-fit lessons.**\n  - The level normaliser must span a full week.\n  - Use ratio-of-sums rather than a clipped mean of ratios.\n  - Use the L1 (|r|-based) form; L2 profiles get destroyed by single crash bars.\n  - Weight recent data (half-life 21 days): the weekday/weekend ratio drifts upward over 2026.\n  - Fit at the scoring step: 5-min returns for 24h, 1-min for 1h.\n- **Adaptive weekend ratio.** Compare the last weekend's deseasonalised L1 level in the context with the context weekdays' level, and multiply the forecast weekend variance by ρ^γ.\n- **Event multipliers.** Applied around macro releases relative to a non-event day. CPI in the eval window: Oct 14 12:30 UTC. PPI + retail sales: Oct 15 12:30. EIA (WTIOIL): Oct 15 16:00 and Oct 21 14:30. No NFP, FOMC or earnings in the eval window.\n- **Field gaps (W_B CRPS ranks).**\n  - c24: about +0.5–0.95% behind the best single miner.\n  - e24: about +0.1–1.2% behind the best; WTIOIL ranks 2/242, XAU 22/242.\n  - c1: +1.9–2.9% behind the best miner, ranks ~193–232 of 242. The field is very compressed.\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n\n**agent/evalrun.py (created)** — batch evaluator.\n- Loads a model file, generates predictions for each asset of a competition in parallel (ProcessPool), and writes npy day layout (`<asset>/<tl>_<ti>/date=YYYY-MM-DD.npy` plus a .json with start_times, float32).\n- Calls the official `backtest(... latest_formula=True, match_tolerance_minutes=cadence or 10)`.\n- Saves per-prompt `scored_time, ours, best, median, q10, asset` to agent/results/<tag>_<comp>.csv and prints a per-asset table plus an ALL line.\n- Arguments: `--model --comp {c24,e24,c1} --assets --start --end --nsim --tag --jobs --cadence --env K=V ...`; the env vars are set before the model is imported.\n- Uses `prices.loc[: context_end(t, tl)][-10080:]`.\n- Harmless \"Exception in thread _monitor\" messages appear at shutdown.\n\n**agent/sweep.sh (created)** — runs several evalrun specs, 3 at a time with --jobs 5.\n```\nagent/sweep.sh START END COMP \"tag:K=V,K=V\" ...\n```\nLogs go to agent/results/log_<tag>_<comp>.txt.\n\n**agent/fit_season.py (created)** — fits the profiles.\n```\nuv run agent/fit_season.py --cutoff D [--start 2026-03-01] --out agent/artifacts/X.json --hl 21 --l1 [--shrink 0.5]\n```\n- Output JSON keys: `nb` (96), `tz`, `cutoff`, `hl`, `profiles_1`, `profiles_5`, `zero_1`, `zero_5` (per asset, 672 values each).\n- fit():\n  - `r = log(c.ffill()).diff(step)`.\n  - `lvl` = rolling 10080 centred (min_periods 5000) mean of r².\n  - keep = finite & ~event_mask.\n  - `z = min(r2, 100*lvl)`.\n  - Bins are keyed on the NY week bin of (index − step//2).\n  - Recency weights `0.5**(age/hl)`.\n  - L1 form: `(Σw√z / Σw√lvl)²`.\n  - Mon–Fri bins are shrunk halfway toward the pooled weekday profile, then normalised to mean 1.\n  - Zero-probability profile: share of `log(c).diff(step) == 0` (both ends traded), with the same bins and weights.\n- `event_mask(idx, asset)` excludes minutes in [−30, +240) around MACRO events (CPI, NFP, FOMC, PPI, GDP, PCE, RETAIL_SALES), plus EIA for WTIOIL. It reads SYNTH_BENCHMARK_CALENDAR; NO_EVENT_MASK disables it.\n\n**Artifacts in agent/artifacts/:** season_pre0908.json, season_pre0908_hl21.json, season_pre0908_l1.json, season_pre0908_hl10_l1.json, season_pre0908_hl21_l1.json, season_pre0908_hl42_l1.json, season_pre0908_hl21_l1_ev.json (event-masked). No season.json exists yet, but the model's default `SEASON_FILE` is \"season.json\". The final artifact must be fitted on all data (cutoff 2026-10-12, --hl 21 --l1, event mask) and saved as season.json.\n\n**agent/modeling.py (rewritten; current state):**\n- Params come from env via `P(name, default)`. Defaults: WINS=30, HL_S=120, HL_L=2880, TAU_MR=240, SCALE=1, NU=5, ETA=0.2, ZK=0.0, WE_SCALE=1, WE_GAMMA=0.0, WE_CRYPTO=0, EVENTS=1, EV_POW=1, EV_SET (prejul or default).\n- `_profiles(fname)` returns (nb, prof{1,5}, zero{1,5}).\n- `_week_minute_profile(asset, idx_utc, step, kind=1|2)`.\n- `CRYPTO` tuple; `_weekend(idx)`: Fri 17:00 → Sun 18:00 NY.\n- `EV_WIN = [-30, 0, 2, 5, 15, 30, 60, 120, 240]`.\n- EV_MULT (all-data medians):\n\n| Event | Multipliers by window |\n|---|---|\n| CPI | [0.85, 26, 5.5, 3.0, 1.8, 1.05, 1.1, 1] |\n| NFP | [0.8, 10, 3.4, 2.3, 1.7, 1.1, 1, 1] |\n| FOMC | [1.0, 10, 4.8, 5.0, 2.35, 3.8, 2.6, 1.3] |\n| GDP | [0.7, 4.8, 1.3, 1.4, 1.15, 1, 1.1, 1] |\n| PCE | [0.7, 4.7, 1.35, 1.45, 1.15, 1, 1.1, 1] |\n| PPI | [0.9, 4.2, 2.2, 2.0, 1.36, 1, 1, 1] |\n| EIA_PETROLEUM | [0.9, 2.0, 1, 1.1, 1, 1, 1, 1] |\n\n- EV_MULT_PREJUL (fitted on releases before 2026-07-01, used for out-of-sample validation): CPI [0.8, 13.6, 5.4, 2.9, 1.27, 1, 1.1, 1], etc.\n- `_calendar(path, mtime)` is cached. `_event_mult(asset, idx_utc)` takes the max of bumps and applies a pre-release lull only where nothing else applies.\n- forecast(asset, start_time, time_increment, time_length, context_prices) → (sig per step, last, p0):\n  - step = 1 if ti < 300 else 5.\n  - `pm = profile*event_mult` over the context.\n  - Overlapping step returns of the ffilled log price; `s_all` = cumulative profile sums.\n  - Cap r2 at WINS×median(r2/s)·s.\n  - `v_s, v_l = _ewma_level(r2c, s, age, HL)`.\n  - lead/k minutes; `lvl = v_l + (v_s - v_l)*exp(-k/TAU_MR)`.\n  - `var_min = profile(fut) * event_mult(fut) * lvl * SCALE²`.\n  - Weekend adjustment: `we_k = WE_SCALE²`; if WE_GAMMA > 0, rho from the context's weekend vs weekday L1 levels, clipped to [0.05, 5], and `we_k *= rho**gam`. It applies to non-crypto assets, or to crypto when WE_CRYPTO > 0.\n  - Per-step variance is summed over minutes. `p0 = zero profile at each step end * ZK`, clipped to 0.9.\n- simulate():\n  - `rng = default_rng(int(SYNTH_BENCHMARK_SEED or 12345))`.\n  - t-innovations normalised to unit variance.\n  - Zero atom via a Bernoulli mask; moving steps are scaled by 1/√(1−p0).\n  - Per-path `m = exp(eta*N - eta²)`.\n  - `inc -= 0.5*(sig*m)²`; paths = last·exp(cumsum), with a leading 0.\n\n**agent/analysis/:**\n- season.py: `load(asset)` helper.\n- vr.py: variance ratios and zero fractions.\n- calib.py: standardised residual diagnostic; supports DUMP=path. Uses `sig, last, _ = m.forecast`.\n- components.py: splits the official score into intervals using calculate_total_score_for_miner.\n- shape.py: proxy CRPS for t/scale/atom shapes.\n- events.py: event-window ratios, saved to /tmp/events.parquet.\n- fieldrank.py: per-miner mean-CRPS rank. Usage: `uv run agent/analysis/fieldrank.py CSV crypto-1h|crypto-24h|com-equ-24h`.\n- paired.py: paired per-prompt comparison split by event. Usage: `paired.py A.csv B.csv [horizon_s]`.\n\n**Other files:**\n- agent/journal.md: entries 0–4 written (setup, v1, zero atom, shape params, weekend). Events and the c1 work are not yet journaled.\n- .gitignore: added `miner_outputs/`.\n- Git: user agent@campaign.local / \"campaign agent\". Two commits so far; the latest is \"profiles L1 hl21, zero atom, adaptive weekend ratio\". Commit messages end with \"Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>\".\n- agent/predict.py: unchanged, still the official single-asset tool.\n\n4. Errors and fixes:\n- Read-only numpy arrays (`P = prof.values.reshape(...)`, `px[0] = last`): fixed with `.copy()`.\n- Missing artifacts/season.json: always pass SEASON_FILE through env/--env.\n- Analysis scripts requested the 2026-10-12 partition: the end is capped at 2026-10-11 23:59.\n- Timezone-naive vs aware error in searchsorted inside event_mask: fixed by converting both sides to naive datetime64[ns].\n- git identity missing: set the repo-local user.\n- Profile bug analysis: the 3-day level window cancelled the weekend effect, and the clipped mean understated the ratio; fixed as described in section 2.\n\n5. Problem Solving — key results (mean CRPS):\n\n| Experiment | Window / config | Result |\n|---|---|---|\n| Starter (log-normal) | 10-04→10-11 | c24 3302 (+11.6% vs median), c1 766 (+15% vs median) |\n| v1 | W_B | c24 3541.5, e24 1772.8, c1 738.8 |\n| Profile variants | e24 W_B | L2hl21 1737.9; L1 1730.5; **L1hl21 1720.6**; L1hl10 1719.3; L1hl42 1724.0 |\n| Zero atom ZK=1 | e24 W_B | 1718.9 |\n| SCALE/NU/ETA sweeps | W_B | all within ±0.3%, flat → defaults kept |\n| Fixed WE_SCALE 0.5 | e24 | B 1709.8, A 1823.8 vs 1819.2 → discarded (sign flips) |\n| Adaptive WE_GAMMA=1 | e24 | A 1818.0, B 1710.3 → kept |\n| WE_CRYPTO=1 | c24 W_B | 3541.1 → 3529.3, all 5 assets better; A not yet validated |\n| WE_CRYPTO | c1 (10-01→10-11) | worse (690.73 → 692.04) |\n| c1 tweaks | c1 | ETA 0.4: 692.27; no atom: 690.61; HL_S 30 + TAU_MR 60: 690.29 (best, marginal); HL_S 30: 691.66; HL_S 60: 691.56; HL_S 15 + TAU 120: 691.39; HL_L 1440: 692.21 |\n| Events (prejul multipliers + event-masked profile), W_A+W_B 09-12→10-11 | e24 / c24 | e24 1762.31 → 1762.06; c24 4008.0 → 4005.8. FOMC prompts −1% (wins 87–100%), CPI −0.3/−0.5% (wins 78–100%), NFP/PCE ≈0. Kept |\n\nOther findings:\n- Shape-proxy analysis: tail shape could gain at most ~0.2% on the 1-min component.\n- The c1 gap is likely in the accuracy of the conditional σ forecast.\n\n6. All user messages:\n- \"Read the CAMPAIGN.md file in your agent folder and start your research campaign.\"\n\n7. Pending Tasks:\n- Improve c1, currently 2–3% behind the best miner. Next idea: range-based (Parkinson) vol in the EWMA.\n- Validate WE_CRYPTO on W_A for c24, and the events on c1.\n- Possibly a HAR-style level fit, or filtered historical simulation by class.\n- Refit the final season.json on all data (cutoff 2026-10-12, hl21, L1, event mask).\n- Bake the chosen defaults into modeling.py: ZK=1, WE_GAMMA=1, WE_CRYPTO only for 24h, events on with all-data EV_MULT, possibly HL_S/TAU_MR for 1h.\n- Measure latency at 1000 paths (currently ~0.05 s/prompt).\n- Run the final per-config CRPS at 1000 paths through agent/predict.py / backtest for both the champion and the starter.\n- Write journal entries (events, c1, field ranks), report.md and suggestions.md.\n- Commit, then create agent/CHAMPION (sha, agent_dir: agent, profiles [low, high], notes with CRPS per config vs starter).\n- Check BUDGET.md every iteration.\n\n8. Current Work:\nI was about to add a range-based (Parkinson) volatility estimator to the EWMA level in agent/modeling.py, aimed at c1's short-window estimation efficiency. Plan:\n- Per-minute PK = (ln H/L)²/(4 ln 2).\n- Calibrate to close-return units with c = Σr²/ΣPK over the context.\n- Blend into v_s/v_l with a parameter RANGE_W.\n\nI had just grepped the relevant lines:\n```\n155: v_s = v_l = 1e-8\n158: r2c = np.minimum(r2, cap * s) if cap > 0 else r2\n159: v_s = _ewma_level(r2c, s, age, P(\"HL_S\", 120))\n160: v_l = _ewma_level(r2c, s, age, P(\"HL_L\", 2880))\n166: lvl = v_l + (v_s - v_l) * np.exp(-k / P(\"TAU_MR\", 240))\n```\nCurrent best c1 configuration for comparison:\n`SEASON_FILE=season_pre0908_hl21_l1.json, ZK=1, WE_GAMMA=1, HL_S=30, TAU_MR=60` (690.29 on 10-01→10-11). Events and the _ev profile have not yet been tested on c1.\n\n9. Optional Next Step:\nImplement the RANGE_W Parkinson blend in forecast(), using the context's high/low columns with NaN-safe handling. Then run, for example:\n```\nagent/sweep.sh 2026-10-01 2026-10-11 c1 \"B1_r0:SEASON_FILE=season_pre0908_hl21_l1_ev.json,ZK=1,WE_GAMMA=1,HL_S=30,TAU_MR=60,EV_SET=prejul\" \"B1_r5:...,RANGE_W=0.5\" \"B1_r10:...,RANGE_W=1\"\n```\nCompare against 690.29, validate on a second window, then journal the events and range results and commit.\n\nIf you need specific details from before compaction (like exact code snippets, error messages, or content you generated), read the full transcript at: /root/.claude/projects/-workspace/fdbca538-ca84-498b-80c3-b8a33e6553ce.jsonl\nContinue the conversation from where it left off without asking the user any further questions. Resume directly — do not acknowledge the summary, do not recap what was happening, do not preface with \"I'll continue\" or similar. Pick up the last task as if the break never happened."}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fdbca538-ca84-498b-80c3-b8a33e6553ce","uuid":"9dab15fd-89d6-4516-b336-6480c4c082af","timestamp":"2026-10-21T14:45:11.772Z","isSynthetic":true}
