{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011CgFioTMECJtgiztoYJYie","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"I've nominated a champion and the campaign is finished. The harness interface check passed for both 24h and 1h. I stopped at 3.1 h and $11.73 of the 18 h / $100, because the last six experiments each moved CRPS by less than 0.1%. Leftover budget is forfeited, but that plateau is the evidence for stopping, and it's written up in the journal.\n\n**What the model is** (`agent/modeling.py` plus one fitted file, `agent/artifacts/season.json`):\n- **Weekly volatility pattern:** 15-minute slots in New York time, recent weeks weighted more, plus a minute-within-the-hour pattern (crypto is busiest right after :00, :15, :30, :45).\n- **Scheduled releases:** variance is scaled up around CPI, FOMC, PPI and similar releases, using dates from the provided calendar.\n- **Current volatility level:** taken from the last 7 days of prices, short-term decaying into long-term.\n- **Equity weekends:** scaled by how quiet the last weekend actually was.\n- **Path shape:** heavy-tailed steps, a chance of the price not moving at all, and some randomness in each path's overall volatility.\n- **Speed:** about 0.05 s per prompt at 1000 paths, on CPU only.\n\n**Results** (official `agent/predict.py`, 1000 paths; 24h on 09-26→10-11, 1h on 09-22→10-11):\n\n| Configuration | Champion | Starter | Change |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| CRYPTO_24H | 3494.1 | 3698.2 | −5.5% |\n| COM_EQU_24H | 1689.2 | 2025.5 | −16.6% |\n| CRYPTO_1H | 801.8 | 853.5 | −6.1% |\n\nThese figures use the served pattern file, which was fitted on data up to 10-11, so they flatter it slightly. When the pattern is fitted only on data from before each window, the gains are −4.5%, −15.8% and −5.4%.\n\nAgainst the single best other miner per asset:\n- **Equities:** within ±0.7%; XAU and SP500 rank 1st, TSLAX and WTIOIL 2nd.\n- **Crypto:** 0.4–1.3% behind. Part of the 1h gap is probably data we don't get rather than the model: the backtest's price history stops 2 minutes before each request, while live miners see prices up to it.\n\n**What made the difference:**\n- **Release scaling** cut CRPS by 5–12% on 1h prompts that contain a CPI, FOMC or PPI release. The 10-day evaluation window includes CPI (10-14) and PPI (10-15).\n- **Release multipliers turned out too weak** as first fitted, and I amplified them. I tested this on July–September releases the multipliers weren't fitted on.\n- **I removed the extra scaling for the weekly oil inventory report (EIA):** it made WTIOIL worse on all 10 test releases, because the weekly pattern already accounts for it.\n\n**What didn't help:** high/low-range volatility estimates, a fitted multi-timescale volatility forecaster, a fixed weekend discount, the weekend adjustment for crypto, and extra variance for long horizons.\n\nEverything is committed: the champion code is at `e764fe5`, and `agent/CHAMPION` is in the commit after it. `journal.md`, `report.md` and `suggestions.md` are in `agent/`, and `starter/` holds the original model with a copy of `predict.py` so the starter numbers can be reproduced."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":1222,"cache_read_input_tokens":132111,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":1222,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":6,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"fdbca538-ca84-498b-80c3-b8a33e6553ce","uuid":"2c9b7c17-999f-414c-ab0e-65d28178921f","timestamp":"2026-10-21T16:46:35.838Z"}
